                <pb facs="1320" n="1310" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/8–2349: Circular Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-23T16:00:00+08:00">August 23, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:01 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Circular. In all cases involving Americans in your district where clear evident
                    lack protection afforded by Communist authorities, you are instructed (1)
                    attempt protest through most effective or feasible channels to local authorities
                    citing circumstances, (2) provide ConGen Peiping and Embassy Nanking with
                    details and recommendation whether or not Peiping should at that time attempt
                    lodge similar protest with Central Communist authorities, (3) repeat information
                    Department. You should keep Embassy Peiping and Department informed re outcome
                    such cases. Re cases concerning which you have initially recommended Peiping not
                    at time protest, you should at any subsequent time you feel such protest
                    desirable recommend such, repeating message to Department. Peiping to keep
                    Embassy, Department and post concerned informed re protests.</p>
                <p>Sent Peiping, Shanghai, Hankow, Department pass Tientsin, Tsingtao.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
